# FastAPI

- Create the app with `create_app()` in `backend/app/main.py`.
- Mount HTTP routes under `/api` through `app/api/`.
- Validate requests and responses with Pydantic schemas in `app/schemas/`.
- Keep SQLAlchemy models in `app/models/` when persistence is added. Do not reuse schemas as ORM models.
- External APIs go behind `app/adapters/{google_places,rentals,geographic}`.
- `POST /api/places/search` retrieves Google Places results through the adapter. Do not scrape Google Maps.
- Do not implement `POST /api/analysis` until metric code exists.

```python
# ❌ BAD
@router.get("/zones")
def list_zones():
    return [{"name": "Castelar", "competitors": 14}]

# ✅ GOOD
@router.get("/health", response_model=HealthResponse)
def get_health() -> HealthResponse:
    return HealthResponse(status="ok")
```
